  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Friction force wil act opposite to the motion of the body.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mtext>-ve&#160;sign&#160;for&#160;direction&#160;relative&#160;to&#160;the&#160;motion&#160;of&#160;body</mtext></mfenced></math></p><p>Now, applying equation of motion, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>50</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></math></p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p>",
